    {
      "issue": "The new foreign-link refusal throws from inside `acs install-model-id` after model-id is already copied and linked and before ask-model is installed (bin/model-id.mjs:132-146 calls installAgent uncaught, then ask-model). So a foreign `~/.local/bin/acs-agent` symlink now aborts the whole command with a raw stack trace and exit 1, ask-model is never installed or updated, and the stale-copy hint keeps telling the user to re-run the same failing command. At base a foreign symlink was replaced and ask-model went on; only the non-symlink case aborted this way.",
      "file": "bin/agent-install.mjs",
      "line": "21",
      "quote": "throw new Error('~/.local/bin/acs-agent points elsewhere — not replacing it');",
      "suggestion": "In bin/model-id.mjs, catch the installAgent error the way the ask-model error is handled: print `model-id: acs-agent was not installed: <message>`, continue to the ask-model install, then exit 1.",
      "likelihood": 2,
      "impact": 3,
      "protected": false,
      "trigger": "`acs install-model-id` when `~/.local/bin/acs-agent` is a symlink to anything but `~/.agent-config-studio/bin/acs-agent`, for example a developer's own link into a checkout.",
      "preExisting": false,
      "risk": 6,
