    },
    {
      "issue": "The new README audit for `acs-agent` accepts commands that do not exist. The verb check on line 57 passes any whole word found anywhere in the usage text, so `acs-agent family`, `acs-agent task`, `acs-agent id`, `acs-agent seconds` and `acs-agent usage` count as documented verbs. The flag check on line 58 is a substring match against the whole help, so `acs-agent list --effort x` passes although `list` has no `--effort`, and a truncated flag such as `--stall` passes because it is inside `--stall-after`. The planted `surely-invalid` cases do not exercise either gap.",
      "file": "tests/readme.mjs",
      "line": "58",
      "quote": "return words.some(w => /^--/.test(w) && w !== '--help' && !agentHelp.stdout.includes(w));",
      "suggestion": "Check words[1] against the verb set parsed from the usage (open, wait, send, answer, close, list), and match flags as whole tokens (`--flag` followed by a space, `]` or end of line), ideally against that verb's own usage line.",
